Subject: [PATCH] tests: skip the default-stack shrink before glibc 2.18

The streaming-cell test lowers glibc's default thread stack to 512 KiB
with pthread_getattr_default_np and pthread_setattr_default_np, which
were added in glibc 2.18. conda-forge compiles against the glibc 2.17
sysroot, so pthread.h does not declare them and test_llvm.cpp fails to
compile:

    test_llvm.cpp:6815:21: error: 'pthread_getattr_default_np' was not
        declared in this scope

Guard the calls with __GLIBC__ and then __GLIBC_PREREQ(2, 18). The
version macro must not be expanded unless __GLIBC__ is defined: Clang
on macOS errors on an undefined function-like macro in #if. On the 2.17
sysroot the test still runs; it just cannot reproduce the small default
stack.

diff --git a/src/lfortran/tests/test_llvm.cpp b/src/lfortran/tests/test_llvm.cpp
index 5aa16fc..54200a6 100644
--- a/src/lfortran/tests/test_llvm.cpp
+++ b/src/lfortran/tests/test_llvm.cpp
@@ -6808,7 +6808,13 @@ TEST_CASE("FortranEvaluator execute: a streaming cell keeps the main thread's st
         MESSAGE("RLIMIT_STACK is below 8 MiB; skipping");
         return;
     }
+// pthread_getattr_default_np and pthread_setattr_default_np were added in
+// glibc 2.18. The conda-forge linux build compiles against the glibc 2.17
+// sysroot, whose pthread.h does not declare them. Keep the __GLIBC__ test
+// outside the version check: Clang rejects an undefined function-like macro
+// in #if, so macOS must not expand __GLIBC_PREREQ.
 #ifdef __GLIBC__
+#if __GLIBC_PREREQ(2, 18)
     struct DefaultStack {
         pthread_attr_t saved;
         DefaultStack() {
@@ -6824,6 +6830,7 @@ TEST_CASE("FortranEvaluator execute: a streaming cell keeps the main thread's st
             pthread_attr_destroy(&saved);
         }
     } default_stack;
+#endif
 #endif
     CompilerOptions cu = execute_options();
     FortranEvaluator e(cu);
